$DIR/main.p:44:15: cannot store arrayProject(refs()) in p, which outlives the temporary
    arrayProject(refs()) points into the temporary [1]synced[Item] that refs()
    returns. The [1]synced[Item] made at main.p:44 is a temporary: nothing keeps
    it, so its object is dropped at the end of the statement. A view of the
    object may be passed to calls in that statement but may not outlive it. At
    the end of the statement, the temporary is dropped, but p lives longer, so
    it would be left pointing at a value that has been dropped.
    The view does not own the memory it looks at. Nothing keeps the temporary
    after the statement, so a stored view would outlive the value that keeps its
    memory alive.
    Keep the owner in a variable, so that it lives until the end of its scope,
    and take the view through that variable:
        v := refs()
        ... v ...
    (see "Views" in the Plutonium spec, section 18.3)
    (run "pluto explain E3009" for a longer explanation)
